---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
import PdfResources from '@/components/PdfResources.astro';
import '@/styles/german-lesson-five.css';
// Reading texts, learning sequence and media follow the open-licensed Grenzenlos Deutsch
// Lektion 6: Hobbys. The short character summaries, exercises and explanations are adaptations.
---
<Base title="German Lesson 6: Hobbys | Listening and practice" description="Beginner German lesson 6: read and listen to four people talking about hobbies, learn gern, conjugate regular verbs and practise with video and exercises.">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/german/lesson-six.css" />
  <div class="lesson-five lesson-six">
    <header class="lesson-hero"><div class="wrap">
      <a href="/resources/german-async#e1" class="back">← Back to your learning path</a>
      <p class="eyebrow">UNIT 01 · LESSON 06 · MAIN LESSON</p>
      <h1 lang="de">Hobbys <em>&amp; Freizeit.</em></h1>
      <p class="intro">Meet four people, listen to them talk about their free time, and learn to say what you like—and do not like—doing.</p>
      <p class="context">Continue from <a href="/resources/german-lesson-5">Lesson 5: Zählen 2</a>. The four listening recordings and the interview video below are from the Creative Commons <a href="https://grenzenlos-deutsch.com/familie/e1/l6/">Grenzenlos Deutsch Lesson 6</a>.</p>
      <nav class="step-nav" aria-label="Lesson sections">
        <a href="#read">01 Read &amp; listen</a><a href="#vocabulary">02 Vocabulary</a><a href="#structures">03 Structures</a><a href="#listening">04 Listening</a><a href="#speaking">05 Speaking</a><a href="#study-resources">06 PDF resource</a>
      </nav>
    </div></header>
    <div class="wrap lesson-body">
      <section id="read" aria-labelledby="read-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">01 / LESEN UND HÖREN</p><h2 id="read-heading">Four people. Four perspectives on free time.</h2>
        <p>Look at each person’s picture. Read the German summary, then use the recording to hear their full account. You can pause or replay each audio clip independently. Audio is streamed from the original course website.</p>
        <div class="people-grid">
          <article class="person-card">
            <img src="/assets/german/img/Yasmin-223x300.png" alt="Portrait of Yasmin from the original German course" loading="lazy" width="223" height="300"/>
            <div class="person-copy"><h3>Yasmin</h3><p class="person-meta">München · 21 Jahre</p><p lang="de">Yasmin spielt gerne Fußball und geht windsurfen. Mit Freundinnen und Freunden spielt sie Karten, hört Musik und geht manchmal tanzen.</p><audio controls preload="none" src="https://grenzenlos-deutsch.com/familie/wp-content/uploads/AUD_Familie_Einheit1_Lektion6_Yasmin.m4a" aria-label="Listen to Yasmin talking about her hobbies">Your browser does not support audio playback.</audio><a class="audio-source" href="https://grenzenlos-deutsch.com/familie/wp-content/uploads/AUD_Familie_Einheit1_Lektion6_Yasmin.m4a">Open Yasmin’s recording</a></div>
          </article>
          <article class="person-card">
            <img src="/assets/german/img/Max.pgn_-211x300.png" alt="Portrait of Max from the original German course" loading="lazy" width="211" height="300"/>
            <div class="person-copy"><h3>Max</h3><p class="person-meta">New York → Wien</p><p lang="de">Max arbeitet am Theater und singt gern. Er besucht Konzerte, schwimmt und fährt Fahrrad. Laufen macht ihm weniger Spaß.</p><audio controls preload="none" src="https://grenzenlos-deutsch.com/familie/wp-content/uploads/AUD_Familie_Einheit1_Lektion6_Max.m4a" aria-label="Listen to Max talking about his hobbies">Your browser does not support audio playback.</audio><a class="audio-source" href="https://grenzenlos-deutsch.com/familie/wp-content/uploads/AUD_Familie_Einheit1_Lektion6_Max.m4a">Open Max’s recording</a></div>
          </article>
          <article class="person-card">
            <img src="/assets/german/img/Johannes.pgn_-211x300.png" alt="Portrait of Johannes from the original German course" loading="lazy" width="211" height="300"/>
            <div class="person-copy"><h3>Johannes</h3><p class="person-meta">Stuttgart · 16 Jahre</p><p lang="de">Johannes liest gerne Bücher und Zeitungen im Café. Außerdem kocht er gern und sieht sich besonders gern internationale Filme im Kino an.</p><audio controls preload="none" src="https://grenzenlos-deutsch.com/familie/wp-content/uploads/AUD_Familie_Einheit1_Lektion6_Johannes.m4a" aria-label="Listen to Johannes talking about his hobbies">Your browser does not support audio playback.</audio><a class="audio-source" href="https://grenzenlos-deutsch.com/familie/wp-content/uploads/AUD_Familie_Einheit1_Lektion6_Johannes.m4a">Open Johannes’s recording</a></div>
          </article>
          <article class="person-card">
            <img src="/assets/german/img/Julia-251x300.png" alt="Portrait of Julia from the original German course" loading="lazy" width="251" height="300"/>
            <div class="person-copy"><h3>Julia</h3><p class="person-meta">Hamburg</p><p lang="de">In ihrer Freizeit macht Julia Spaziergänge im Park. Sie fotografiert gerne die Natur und interessiert sich für Kunst und Fotografie.</p><audio controls preload="none" src="https://grenzenlos-deutsch.com/familie/wp-content/uploads/AUD_Familie_Einheit1_Lektion6_Julia.m4a" aria-label="Listen to Julia talking about her hobbies">Your browser does not support audio playback.</audio><a class="audio-source" href="https://grenzenlos-deutsch.com/familie/wp-content/uploads/AUD_Familie_Einheit1_Lektion6_Julia.m4a">Open Julia’s recording</a></div>
          </article>
        </div>
        <p class="small">These four audio tracks are hosted externally by Grenzenlos Deutsch, so playback and direct downloads require internet access. If an audio player fails, use its “Open recording” link.</p>
        <h3 class="subheading">Check your understanding</h3>
        <p>Select an answer for each question, then check your responses. These are new practice questions based on the four profiles.</p>
        <form class="auto-quiz quiz-form" id="hobby-reading-quiz">
          <fieldset data-answer="Yasmin"><legend>01 · Wer spielt gern Fußball?</legend><div class="choices"><label><input type="radio" name="q1" value="Yasmin"/> Yasmin</label><label><input type="radio" name="q1" value="Julia"/> Julia</label><label><input type="radio" name="q1" value="Johannes"/> Johannes</label></div><p class="feedback" aria-live="polite"></p></fieldset>
          <fieldset data-answer="Max"><legend>02 · Wer arbeitet beim Theater?</legend><div class="choices"><label><input type="radio" name="q2" value="Johannes"/> Johannes</label><label><input type="radio" name="q2" value="Max"/> Max</label><label><input type="radio" name="q2" value="Yasmin"/> Yasmin</label></div><p class="feedback" aria-live="polite"></p></fieldset>
          <fieldset data-answer="Johannes"><legend>03 · Wer liest gern im Café?</legend><div class="choices"><label><input type="radio" name="q3" value="Julia"/> Julia</label><label><input type="radio" name="q3" value="Yasmin"/> Yasmin</label><label><input type="radio" name="q3" value="Johannes"/> Johannes</label></div><p class="feedback" aria-live="polite"></p></fieldset>
          <fieldset data-answer="Julia"><legend>04 · Wer fotografiert gern die Natur?</legend><div class="choices"><label><input type="radio" name="q4" value="Julia"/> Julia</label><label><input type="radio" name="q4" value="Max"/> Max</label><label><input type="radio" name="q4" value="Johannes"/> Johannes</label></div><p class="feedback" aria-live="polite"></p></fieldset>
          <div class="quiz-actions"><button type="submit">Check my answers</button><button type="reset" class="secondary">Try again</button></div><p class="quiz-score" role="status"></p>
        </form>
      </section>
      <section id="vocabulary" aria-labelledby="vocab-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">02 / WORTSCHATZ</p><h2 id="vocab-heading">Talk about your hobbies.</h2>
        <p>Many hobbies are expressed using a verb. Some expressions combine <em lang="de">gehen</em> (“to go”) with an activity or destination.</p>
        <div class="grammar-grid"><article><h3>Activities</h3><ul><li><span lang="de">Fußball spielen</span> — play football</li><li><span lang="de">Karten spielen</span> — play cards</li><li><span lang="de">Musik hören</span> — listen to music</li><li><span lang="de">Bücher lesen</span> — read books</li><li><span lang="de">kochen</span> — cook</li><li><span lang="de">singen</span> — sing</li><li><span lang="de">tanzen</span> — dance</li><li><span lang="de">fotografieren</span> — take photographs</li></ul></article><article><h3>Going places</h3><ul><li><span lang="de">ins Kino gehen</span> — go to the cinema</li><li><span lang="de">ins Konzert gehen</span> — go to a concert</li><li><span lang="de">ins Museum gehen</span> — go to a museum</li><li><span lang="de">spazieren gehen</span> — go for a walk</li><li><span lang="de">Fahrrad fahren</span> — go cycling</li><li><span lang="de">schwimmen gehen</span> — go swimming</li><li><span lang="de">eine Ausstellung besuchen</span> — visit an exhibition</li></ul></article></div>
        <p class="tip"><strong>Notice:</strong> Some expressions use two verbs. For example, <em lang="de">Ich gehe gern schwimmen</em> means “I like to go swimming.”</p>
      </section>
      <section id="structures" aria-labelledby="structure-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">03 / STRUKTUREN</p><h2 id="structure-heading">Verbs, <em lang="de">gern</em> and <em lang="de">nicht gern</em>.</h2>
        <p>Add <strong lang="de">gern</strong> to say you enjoy an activity. Use <strong lang="de">nicht gern</strong> to say you do not enjoy it.</p>
        <div class="dialogue"><p lang="de">Ich lese gern. <span class="translation">— I like reading.</span></p><p lang="de">Ich laufe nicht gern. <span class="translation">— I do not like running.</span></p><p lang="de">Was machst du besonders gern? <span class="translation">— What do you especially like doing?</span></p></div>
        <h3 class="subheading">Regular present-tense endings</h3>
        <div class="table-wrap"><table><caption>Example verb: spielen (to play)</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Person</th><th scope="col">Form</th><th scope="col">Example</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td lang="de">ich</td><td lang="de">spiele</td><td lang="de">Ich spiele gern Karten.</td></tr><tr><td lang="de">du</td><td lang="de">spielst</td><td lang="de">Du spielst Fußball.</td></tr><tr><td lang="de">er / sie / es</td><td lang="de">spielt</td><td lang="de">Sie spielt gern.</td></tr><tr><td lang="de">wir</td><td lang="de">spielen</td><td lang="de">Wir spielen zusammen.</td></tr><tr><td lang="de">ihr</td><td lang="de">spielt</td><td lang="de">Ihr spielt Karten.</td></tr><tr><td lang="de">sie / Sie</td><td lang="de">spielen</td><td lang="de">Sie spielen gerne.</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
        <p class="small">Some frequent hobby verbs are irregular or have spelling changes (for example, <em lang="de">lesen → du liest</em>, <em lang="de">fahren → du fährst</em>). The endings above illustrate a regular verb.</p>
        <h3 class="subheading">Apply the forms</h3><form class="auto-quiz quiz-form" id="hobby-grammar-quiz">
          <fieldset data-answer="spiele"><legend>01 · Ich ___ Fußball.</legend><div class="choices"><label><input type="radio" name="g1" value="spiele"/> spiele</label><label><input type="radio" name="g1" value="spielst"/> spielst</label><label><input type="radio" name="g1" value="spielt"/> spielt</label></div><p class="feedback" aria-live="polite"></p></fieldset>
          <fieldset data-answer="spielt"><legend>02 · Julia ___ gern Karten.</legend><div class="choices"><label><input type="radio" name="g2" value="spielen"/> spielen</label><label><input type="radio" name="g2" value="spielt"/> spielt</label><label><input type="radio" name="g2" value="spielst"/> spielst</label></div><p class="feedback" aria-live="polite"></p></fieldset>
          <fieldset data-answer="gern"><legend>03 · Which word means you <strong>like</strong> an activity?</legend><div class="choices"><label><input type="radio" name="g3" value="nicht"/> nicht</label><label><input type="radio" name="g3" value="gern"/> gern</label><label><input type="radio" name="g3" value="kein"/> kein</label></div><p class="feedback" aria-live="polite"></p></fieldset>
          <div class="quiz-actions"><button type="submit">Check my answers</button><button type="reset" class="secondary">Try again</button></div><p class="quiz-score" role="status"></p>
        </form>
      </section>
      <section id="listening" aria-labelledby="listen-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">04 / HÖREN</p><h2 id="listen-heading">Listen to the hobby interviews.</h2>
        <p>Watch the video and identify hobbies mentioned by the interviewees. Replay parts that are difficult and note down the verbs you recognise.</p>
        <div class="video"><iframe title="Grenzenlos Deutsch, Lesson 6: Hobbys – interview video" src="https://player.vimeo.com/video/288174431?h=f5320feff7" loading="lazy" referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" allow="autoplay; fullscreen; picture-in-picture; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; web-share" allowfullscreen></iframe></div>
        <p class="small">The embedded Vimeo interview requires internet. <a href="https://player.vimeo.com/video/288174431?h=f5320feff7">Open the video directly</a> if the player does not load.</p>
        <div class="tip"><strong>Listening strategy:</strong> On the first listen, focus on words such as <em lang="de">spielen</em>, <em lang="de">schwimmen</em> and <em lang="de">singen</em>. On the second listen, notice who enjoys each activity.</div>
      </section>
      <section id="speaking" aria-labelledby="speaking-heading"><p class="eyebrow">05 / SPRECHEN</p><h2 id="speaking-heading">Find out what your partner enjoys.</h2><ol class="speaking"><li><strong lang="de">Welche Hobbys findest du interessant?</strong><span>Which of the four people's hobbies interest you? Which do not?</span></li><li><strong lang="de">Was machst du besonders gern? Was machst du nicht gern?</strong><span>Answer both questions using two or three full sentences.</span></li><li><strong lang="de">Wer spielt gern Fußball? Wer hört gern Musik?</strong><span>Find someone in your class or group who likes sports, music, cycling, singing, writing or swimming.</span></li><li><strong lang="de">Rollenspiel</strong><span>Interview a partner as if they were one of the people from the video. Ask what they do in their free time.</span></li></ol><a class="next" href="/resources/german-lesson-7">Continue to Lesson 7 →</a></section>
